window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>In the rugged highlands of ancient Scotland, a sacred duty binds one clan to an eternal purpose. Uilleam Madadhallaidh, a young man burdened by tragedy and exile, discovers his lineage ties him to the Clan of the Wolf—a secretive brotherhood sworn to protect the most sacred artifact in history: the Ark of the Covenant.</p> <p>Through a mystical transformation, Uilleam becomes the first of his kind—a werewolf warrior blessed with immense strength and tasked with a divine mission. As he forges his clan from outcasts, warriors, and seekers of purpose, Uilleam must battle the encroaching forces of the Roman Empire and a shadowy cult known as the Children of Cain, who will stop at nothing to seize the Ark's power.</p> <p>Amidst treachery, loyalty, and the struggle for survival, the Clan of the Wolf builds their stronghold, uniting ancient traditions, divine intervention, and fierce determination. As Uilleam’s legacy takes root, the clan’s howls echo through the misty highlands, a haunting reminder of their sacred oath and the price of keeping the darkness at bay.</p> <p>Blending historical drama, mysticism, and the unyielding spirit of the Scottish Highlands, <i>Werewolves of Scotland</i> is a tale of sacrifice, redemption, and the indomitable strength of a people united under a celestial calling.</p>"; 
